cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite the accompanying manuscript."
title: "HaluRISC: Calibrated Hallucination Risk Scoring for Large Language Models"
abstract: "HaluRISC is a black-box hallucination risk scorer. It combines evidence-aware text features, a calibrated XGBoost classifier, claim-level natural language inference aggregates, and SHAP explanations. The repository includes the feature pipeline, the FastAPI inference service, the Next.js dashboard, and the reproducible evaluation code."
